From: V-PACE <yocto@vpace>
Subject: [PATCH] steering_odometry: split steering-axle track from traction-axle track

SteeringOdometry keeps a single wheel_track_ and uses it for two physically
different quantities:

  - the driven (traction) axle's differential-speed geometry
    (get_linear_velocity_double_traction_axle(), and the Wr/Wl traction
    commands in get_commands() for TRICYCLE_CONFIG/ACKERMANN_CONFIG), and

  - the steered axle's angle geometry: converting a single "bicycle" steer
    angle into the two individual wheel angles and back
    (update_from_velocity()'s right/left steer_pos_est, and the
    alpha_r/alpha_l split in get_commands() for ACKERMANN_CONFIG).

For the second use, the correct track is the spacing between the two
steered kingpins -- deriving the standard Ackermann relation
tan(delta) = L / (R -+ T/2) for the individual wheel gives exactly the code
already there, but only if T is the steered axle's own track. The traction
axle's track has no part in that geometry.

ackermann_steering_controller::configure_odometry() only ever calls
set_wheel_params() with one track (front_wheel_track when
front_steering=false, else rear_wheel_track), so today every steering-angle
calculation silently uses the *traction* axle's track instead of the
*steering* axle's. This is exact only when front_wheel_track ==
rear_wheel_track, and grows with commanded steering angle otherwise
(confirmed against measured hardware: a vehicle with front_wheel_track
0.12 m and rear_wheel_track 0.18179 m showed a real average-steering-angle
readout that only matches the existing rear_wheel_track-based formula, off
by 1.3e-3 rad from the geometrically-correct front-track formula at a 0.25
rad commanded angle).

This is already fixed upstream on the kilted branch by splitting the
odometry into wheel_track_steering_/wheel_track_traction_ (as part of the
larger SteeringOdometry -> SteeringKinematics rework). That rework depends
on newer hardware_interface handle APIs (LoanedStateInterface::
get_optional()) not present in Humble, so it cannot be cherry-picked as-is.
This patch backports just the track-width split, keeping Humble's existing
class/API surface (LoanedStateInterface::get_value(), no
steering_kinematics rename):

  - adds wheel_track_traction_ alongside the existing wheel_track_ (which
    now means "steering track"),
  - adds a 4-arg set_wheel_params(wheel_radius, wheelbase,
    wheel_track_steering, wheel_track_traction) overload; the existing
    3-arg overload sets both to the same value, so bicycle/tricycle
    single-track callers are unaffected,
  - repoints the three traction differential-speed call sites at
    wheel_track_traction_, leaving the steer-angle formulas on
    wheel_track_ (steering track) untouched.

See the companion patch to ackermann_steering_controller for the call-site
change that actually passes both tracks.

Verified against steering_controllers_library 2.52.1-1 (release/humble),
ros2-gbp/ros2_controllers-release @ e966ebd97fb3aebd294500734762202c05834463.

diff --git a/include/steering_controllers_library/steering_odometry.hpp b/include/steering_controllers_library/steering_odometry.hpp
--- a/include/steering_controllers_library/steering_odometry.hpp
+++ b/include/steering_controllers_library/steering_odometry.hpp
@@ -170,12 +170,24 @@
   double get_angular() const { return angular_; }

   /**
-   * \brief Sets the wheel parameters: radius, separation and wheelbase
+   * \brief Sets the wheel parameters: radius, separation and wheelbase.
+   * Sets both the steering-axle and traction-axle track to \p wheel_track.
    */
   void set_wheel_params(
     const double wheel_radius, const double wheelbase = 0.0, const double wheel_track = 0.0);

   /**
+   * \brief Sets the wheel parameters with separate steering-axle and traction-axle track
+   * widths. Ackermann vehicles use the steering-axle track (the actual spacing between the
+   * two steered kingpins) for the steer-angle geometry, and the traction-axle track for the
+   * driven-wheel differential-speed geometry -- these differ whenever front and rear track
+   * are not equal.
+   */
+  void set_wheel_params(
+    const double wheel_radius, const double wheelbase, const double wheel_track_steering,
+    const double wheel_track_traction);
+
+  /**
    * \brief Velocity rolling window size setter
    * \param velocity_rolling_window_size Velocity rolling window size
    */
@@ -260,9 +272,10 @@
   double angular_;  // [rad/s]

   /// Kinematic parameters
-  double wheel_track_;   // [m]
-  double wheelbase_;     // [m]
-  double wheel_radius_;  // [m]
+  double wheel_track_;            // [m] steering-axle track (steered kingpin spacing)
+  double wheel_track_traction_;   // [m] traction-axle track (driven-wheel spacing)
+  double wheelbase_;              // [m]
+  double wheel_radius_;           // [m]

   /// Configuration type used for the forward kinematics
   int config_type_ = -1;

diff --git a/src/steering_odometry.cpp b/src/steering_odometry.cpp
--- a/src/steering_odometry.cpp
+++ b/src/steering_odometry.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
   linear_(0.0),
   angular_(0.0),
   wheel_track_(0.0),
+  wheel_track_traction_(0.0),
   wheelbase_(0.0),
   wheel_radius_(0.0),
   traction_wheel_old_pos_(0.0),
@@ -143,8 +144,10 @@
   }

   // overdetermined, we take the average
-  const double vel_r = vel_wheel_r * turning_radius / (turning_radius + wheel_track_ * 0.5);
-  const double vel_l = vel_wheel_l * turning_radius / (turning_radius - wheel_track_ * 0.5);
+  const double vel_r =
+    vel_wheel_r * turning_radius / (turning_radius + wheel_track_traction_ * 0.5);
+  const double vel_l =
+    vel_wheel_l * turning_radius / (turning_radius - wheel_track_traction_ * 0.5);
   return (vel_r + vel_l) * 0.5;
 }

@@ -196,6 +199,16 @@
   wheel_radius_ = wheel_radius;
   wheelbase_ = wheelbase;
   wheel_track_ = wheel_track;
+  wheel_track_traction_ = wheel_track;
+}
+
+void SteeringOdometry::set_wheel_params(
+  double wheel_radius, double wheelbase, double wheel_track_steering, double wheel_track_traction)
+{
+  wheel_radius_ = wheel_radius;
+  wheelbase_ = wheelbase;
+  wheel_track_ = wheel_track_steering;
+  wheel_track_traction_ = wheel_track_traction;
 }

 void SteeringOdometry::set_velocity_rolling_window_size(size_t velocity_rolling_window_size)
@@ -288,8 +301,8 @@
